<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Guards (Russia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-guards-finland">Red Guards</a> were armed workers' militias formed in Russian cities in 1917 and controlled by the Bolsheviks. They helped seize power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a> and spread Soviet rule to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, often with great violence, as at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> in 1918. They were absorbed into the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> during 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-guards-russia.jpg" alt="Red Guards (Russia)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
